<div class="margin-y-2" markdown="1">

{%- assign tool_key = include.tool_key -%}
{%- assign tool_meta = page.tools[tool_key] -%}
{%- assign exec_name = include.exec | default: include.tool | default: tool_meta.exec | default: page.tool | default: "tool_name" -%}
{%- assign exec_suffix = exec_name | slice: -3, 3 -%}
{%- if include.version_cmd -%}
  {%- assign version_cmd = include.version_cmd -%}
{%- elsif tool_meta.version_cmd -%}
  {%- assign version_cmd = tool_meta.version_cmd -%}
{%- elsif exec_suffix == ".sh" -%}
  {%- assign version_cmd = nil -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign version_cmd = exec_name | append: " --version" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if include.help_cmd -%}
  {%- assign help_cmd = include.help_cmd -%}
{%- elsif tool_meta.help_cmd -%}
  {%- assign help_cmd = tool_meta.help_cmd -%}
{%- elsif exec_suffix == ".sh" -%}
  {%- assign help_cmd = exec_name -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign help_cmd = exec_name | append: " --help" -%}
{%- endif -%}

Verify that the tool is available and responding before running further steps:

```bash
command -v {{ exec_name }}   # command path
{%- if version_cmd %}
{{ version_cmd }}   # version
{%- endif %}
{%- if help_cmd %}
{{ help_cmd }}   # basic usage and options
{%- endif %}
```
{% if include.skip != "true" %}
<small>**NOTE:** *Record the actual tool version in your `README` or project notes so the setup can be reproduced later.*</small>
{% endif %}
</div>
